    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "We can break down evaluation scores into a mean component and a random component. By using the Central Limit Theorem, we can estimate the standard error of the mean score. <strong>This allows us to compute confidence intervals and determine the significance of differences between models</strong>. We also discuss how to handle clustered questions, where multiple questions are related to the same topic or context.",
