    {
      "title": "The Results",
      "content": "By applying our framework to a hypothetical example, we can see how adding error bars to evaluation scores changes our interpretation of the results. <strong>We find that differences between models are not always statistically significant, and that the uncertainty in the scores can be substantial</strong>. This highlights the importance of considering error bars when comparing language models.",
